course: dictionary
lesson: 14373
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Ordained» can mean made a priest in a special ceremony, ordered by someone with power, or decided by fate or God. The words around it show you which meaning is right.
explain: «Ayo was ordained as a minister in the church last Sunday.» The words church and minister are the clues. Ordained means made a religious leader in a ceremony.
explain: «The king's new rule was ordained by the council.» There is no church here. A rule, a king and a council are clues that ordained means ordered or decided by someone with power.
explain: «It was ordained that the two friends would meet again.» This one is about fate: it was meant to happen. Always ask which meaning fits, then try it in the sentence.
fact: Ordained is a verb form of ordain: ordain, ordains, ordained, ordaining.
fact: «Ordained» means made a priest, minister or religious leader in a special ceremony.
fact: «Ordained» can mean ordered or decided by someone with power, like a law or a king.
fact: «Ordained» can also mean decided by fate or by God, as in «divinely ordained».
fact: Useful phrases: «be ordained a priest», «ordained minister», «divinely ordained».
exercise: «The bishop ordained her as a priest in the cathedral.» What does ordained mean here? | Painted in gold | Ordered by a king | *Made a priest in a special ceremony | Lost in the crowd
exercise: «The rule was ordained by the queen, so everyone had to follow it.» What does ordained mean here? | Made a priest in a ceremony | Hidden in a box | *Ordered by someone with power | Fixed with glue
exercise: «Some people believe their lives are divinely ordained.» What does divinely ordained suggest? | Made of wood | *Decided by fate or by God | Very old | Lost in a storm
test: «He was ordained as a minister after years of study.» What does ordained mean? | *Made a religious leader in a special ceremony | Lost in a forest | Ordered by a king
test: «It was ordained that the storm would pass by evening.» What does ordained suggest? | *Decided by fate, as if it was meant to happen | Stolen | Brightly painted
exam: Which sentence uses «ordained» to mean ordered by someone with power? | *«The king ordained that all shops must close on Sunday.» | «She was ordained a minister in May.» | «The dog ordained the stick.» | «The ordained path led up the hill.»
